# Context: 1M tokens (HUGE - can ingest entire codebases)
# Strengths: Fast, cheap, massive context
# Weaknesses: Goes off-rails, makes unauthorized changes, deletes things
# Safety: Default runs without --yolo; add it manually if needed
# Docs: https://geminicli.com/docs
#
# Approval mode defaults to "default" (prompts for approval). To reduce prompt
# spam while keeping approval mode default, allow common safe tools.
#
# Note: tool names are Gemini-internal; adjust based on the approval prompt UI
# if your Gemini version uses different identifiers.
#
# Interactive mode: -i/--prompt-interactive requires a prompt string argument
# (and cannot be used with stdin piping), so we use ##PROMPT## here.
gemini --allowed-tools shell --allowed-tools read_file --allowed-tools write_file --allowed-tools edit_file --allowed-tools apply_patch --allowed-tools list_directory --allowed-tools search -i ##PROMPT##
